%% Resource resolution and cache lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> NoSurface: CanvasRuntime active

  state "No active surface session" as NoSurface
  note right of NoSurface
    Resource descriptors remain committed document input.
    Runtime resource orchestration can publish dirty-resource
    repaint state, but there is no resource-asset session cache to retain.
  end note

  NoSurface --> ActiveSession: successful CanvasSurface attach / create SurfaceResourceSession
  NoSurface --> NoSurfaceDirtySignal: markResourceDirty(id) or markAllResourcesDirty()
  NoSurface --> Disposed: dispose()

  state "No-surface dirty signal" as NoSurfaceDirtySignal
  note right of NoSurfaceDirtySignal
    Dirty-resource calls still publish public resourceVisual state
    and main repaint intent without an attached surface. There is
    no session cache to invalidate; the next attach starts empty.
  end note
  NoSurfaceDirtySignal --> NoSurface: increment public resource visual revision and publish state

  state "Active SurfaceResourceSession" as ActiveSession
  note right of ActiveSession
    SurfaceResourceSession owns the surface resolver reference,
    resolverGeneration, ResourceAssetCache, typed resource-asset resolution,
    per-frame resolver budget,
    same-frame null-result suppression, and budget follow-up throttle.
    Missing descriptors and absent resolvers return bounded placeholders.
    Target/all/replacement/reset/drop first release session cache/suppression
    borrows, then invoke the identity-aware CanvasSurface callback to release
    matching retained main-output image/vector wrapper borrows.
    There is no file, network, remote, or asset-bundle IO.
  end note

  ActiveSession --> ResolveRequested: main paint record carries resourceId
  ActiveSession --> ActiveSession: rejected second surface attach / existing session remains alive
  ActiveSession --> ResolverReplaced: CanvasSurface calls replaceResolver
  ActiveSession --> DescriptorMutation: accepted CanvasEdit mutates descriptors
  ActiveSession --> DocumentReset: accepted loadDocumentFromJson replaces the document
  ActiveSession --> DirtySignal: markResourceDirty(id) or markAllResourcesDirty()
  ActiveSession --> DroppingSession: detach or runtime swap / lifecycle drop
  ActiveSession --> Disposed: dispose() / lifecycle drop

  ResolverReplaced --> ActiveSession: install resolver and increment resolverGeneration; clear cache/suppression/pending budget follow-up; then release identity-aware retained output

  state "Document replacement reset" as DocumentReset
  DocumentReset --> ActiveSession: RuntimeRoot calls lifecycle reset; session and retained-output borrows release before publication

  state "Dropping active session" as DroppingSession
  DroppingSession --> NoSurface: lifecycle drop releases session cache/suppression, then retained output, before return

  state "Resolve request" as ResolveRequested
  ResolveRequested --> DescriptorSnapshot: Frame asks FrameFactsPort for descriptor facts

  state "Descriptor snapshot" as DescriptorSnapshot
  note right of DescriptorSnapshot
    FrameFactsPort reads committed resource descriptors from the
    committed-state owner and passes sealed immutable image/vector descriptor facts
    to the session boundary.
    The resolver cannot create, remove, or update descriptors.
  end note

  DescriptorSnapshot --> MissingDescriptor: descriptor missing
  DescriptorSnapshot --> AppKeyDescriptor: image/vector descriptor source is appKey

  state "Missing descriptor" as MissingDescriptor
  MissingDescriptor --> PlaceholderResult: return bounded placeholder

  state "appKey descriptor available" as AppKeyDescriptor
  note right of AppKeyDescriptor
    v1 descriptors expose app-owned resource identity:
    resourceId plus CanvasAppKeyResourceSource.key
    and descriptor CanvasMetadata.
  end note

  AppKeyDescriptor --> CacheLookup: lookup ResourceAssetCache

  state "Cache lookup" as CacheLookup
  note right of CacheLookup
    ResourceAssetCache identity is keyed strictly by
    resolverGeneration + resourceId + resourceRevision.
    Image byte and vector-zero-byte admission are policy-owned; descriptor byteLength
    remains descriptor metadata, not cache pressure truth.
    Dirty-resource operations release affected/all active-session
    cache/suppression borrows, then matching retained main-output borrows,
    before public publication.
  end note

  CacheLookup --> CachedResolved: cache hit with typed asset
  CacheLookup --> SameFrameSuppressed: same-frame null result already seen
  CacheLookup --> CacheMiss: cache miss

  state "Cached resolved result" as CachedResolved
  CachedResolved --> ResolvedVisual: use app-owned asset reference

  state "Same-frame suppressed result" as SameFrameSuppressed
  SameFrameSuppressed --> PlaceholderResult: use bounded placeholder

  state "Cache miss" as CacheMiss
  CacheMiss --> ResolverBudgetGate: check per-frame resolver budget

  state "Resolver budget gate" as ResolverBudgetGate
  note right of ResolverBudgetGate
    The fixed per-frame guard limits resolver callbacks. Budget-exceeded
    results paint placeholders and may schedule at most one
    pending throttled follow-up repaint. The session owns
    that throttle and clears the pending flag on the next
    main frame resource pass. Painters and app resolvers must not
    schedule budget-exceeded follow-up repaints. Budget-exceeded
    results are not cached as null, missing, or resolved assets.
  end note

  ResolverBudgetGate --> BudgetExceededPlaceholder: budget exhausted
  ResolverBudgetGate --> SyncResolverCall: budget available

  state "Budget-exceeded placeholder" as BudgetExceededPlaceholder
  BudgetExceededPlaceholder --> PlaceholderResult: return bounded placeholder without cache write

  state "Synchronous app resolver call" as SyncResolverCall
  note right of SyncResolverCall
    The session is the only resource-asset resolution boundary in paint.
    Resolver calls are synchronous, app-owned, and must not mutate runtime,
    Store, SelectionKernel, CanvasDocument, descriptors, or preview.
  end note

  SyncResolverCall --> ReentrantMutationRejected: app attempts public runtime mutation
  SyncResolverCall --> ResolverExceptionResult: app throws ordinary exception
  SyncResolverCall --> NullResult: app returns null
  SyncResolverCall --> ResolvedResult: app returns image/vector asset

  state "Reentrant mutation rejected" as ReentrantMutationRejected
  note right of ReentrantMutationRejected
    Public runtime mutation from inside the resolver throws
    StateError and produces no document, selection-owner, preview,
    cache, repaint, or action effect.
  end note
  ReentrantMutationRejected --> SyncResolverCall: resolver continues or unwinds without accepted mutation

  state "Resolver exception placeholder" as ResolverExceptionResult
  note right of ResolverExceptionResult
    Ordinary app resolver failures, including ordinary StateError
    failures, degrade only this resource to a bounded placeholder.
    The result consumes resolver budget but is not cached, not
    null-suppressed, and does not write DiagnosticsHub. Later frames
    may retry the app resolver. Runtime resolver guard rejections
    remain fail-fast StateError failures instead.
  end note
  ResolverExceptionResult --> PlaceholderResult: return bounded placeholder

  state "Null resolver result" as NullResult
  NullResult --> SameFrameNullSuppression: remember null result for current frame key(resolverGeneration, resourceId, resourceRevision) only
  SameFrameNullSuppression --> PlaceholderResult: return bounded placeholder

  state "Resolved resolver result" as ResolvedResult
  ResolvedResult --> CacheResolvedResult: derive current asset weight and admit by key
  state "Oversized resolved result" as OversizedResolvedResult
  CacheResolvedResult --> OversizedResolvedResult: current asset exceeds policy admission
  CacheResolvedResult --> ResolvedVisual: return resolved visual
  OversizedResolvedResult --> ResolvedVisual: return current asset without retention

  state "Resolved visual" as ResolvedVisual
  note right of ResolvedVisual
    The session cache and CanvasSurface retained main output may
    temporarily borrow the reference for paint, but the application
    owns the asset and its disposal. The engine never owns or
    disposes app-provided ui.Image, CanvasPreparedVector, or the
    prepared vector's private Picture.
  end note
  ResolvedVisual --> ActiveSession: paint completes

  state "Placeholder fallback" as PlaceholderResult
  note right of PlaceholderResult
    Missing descriptors, resolver exceptions, and unresolved/null results paint a
    bounded placeholder. They do not trigger full-document
    repaint loops. Null results suppress only same-frame retries;
    resolver exceptions remain retryable on later frames.
  end note
  PlaceholderResult --> ActiveSession: paint completes

  state "Descriptor mutation path" as DescriptorMutation
  note left of DescriptorMutation
    Descriptor mutation is admitted only through normal
    rollback-safe edit or staged load. It is not a resolver
    side channel.
  end note
  DescriptorMutation --> DescriptorRevisionChanged: atomic install succeeds
  DescriptorRevisionChanged --> DescriptorCacheReleased: release target/all session cache/suppression and retained main-output borrows
  DescriptorCacheReleased --> ActiveSession: main repaint if used

  state "Resource dirty signal" as DirtySignal
  note left of DirtySignal
    Dirty marks external visual content stale only.
    It does not mutate CanvasDocument, resource descriptors,
    selection, preview, or action streams.
  end note
  DirtySignal --> VisualRevisionChanged: accept dirty and increment resourceVisualRevision
  VisualRevisionChanged --> DirtyResourceReleased: release target resource or all session cache/suppression and retained main-output borrows before publication
  DirtyResourceReleased --> ActiveSession: publish CanvasRuntimeState and schedule main repaint

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  note right of Disposed
    Dispose drops any active SurfaceResourceSession after its cache/suppression
    and retained main-output wrapper borrows release, without disposing
    app-owned ui.Image, CanvasPreparedVector, or a prepared vector's private
    Picture. Later resource resolution cannot revive session state, call the
    app resolver, or mutate Store.
  end note
  Disposed --> Disposed: dispose again / no side effects
  Disposed --> Disposed: later resolve, dirty signal, edit, load, or pointer input / StateError

  note left of ActiveSession
    Negative invariants:
    no engine-owned file, network, asset-bundle, or remote load,
    no sync glue between duplicate resource sources,
    no direct Store mutation from CanvasResourceResolver,
    no accepted public runtime mutation from inside resolver,
    no document action from resource dirty invalidation,
    no descriptor mutation outside edit/load path,
  end note
